From 5eee76b5acbbd549110c57c8e7868f7cd07e416f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RVZO6 <66844656+RVZO6@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 09:29:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 71/76] Formats/XMA: add 10-bit VLC lookup table, u64 bit-peek,
 and quant-factor LUT

Speed up XMA2 frame decoding without changing decoded bits:
- Bits::peek32 reads a single unaligned u64::from_be_bytes word on the hot
  path (>= 8 bytes left) with a 5-byte tail fallback.
- Vlc::new builds a 10-bit primary lookup table (Box<[(i32, u8); 1024]>)
  covering >99% of Huffman symbols in O(1), falling back to a prefix-bounded
  binary search for codes longer than 10 bits.
- quant_factor caches 10^(exp / 16) in a bit-exact OnceLock<[f32; 384]> LUT
  for exp in -128..256 (matching 10.0_f32.powf(exp as f32 / 16.0) to_bits).

Measured (--release vlc_and_quant_throughput):
- vlc coef0: 28.09 -> 6.30 ns/sym (4.46x)
- vlc coef1: 23.47 -> 5.86 ns/sym (4.00x)
- vlc vec4:  23.76 -> 5.58 ns/sym (4.26x)
- quant:     10.69 -> 1.18 ns/op  (9.05x)

Assisted-by: T3 Code (Antigravity, gemini-4-neon)
